  "captions": {
    "current_architecture": "Source-bound conceptual TSH2 data flow. Laptop and HPS boxes execute on CPUs; the middle boundary is FPGA fabric. The two HPS boxes describe feeding and draining within one service. THR2 is configurable before a finite epoch and fixed during it. This is not a live-codec or FPGA-DDR streaming diagram, and no stage timing is inferred.",
    "flute_captured_spectrograms": "Diagnostic STFT of the registered flute input and actual physical FPGA outputs from epochs 49, 51 and 57. Trial 1 at each threshold is byte-identical. Y is aligned by exactly 384 samples; the displayed support is 384,000 samples. Fixed periodic Hann window, hop, FFT, full 0 to 24 kHz frequency range and -100 to -20 dBFS color range are shared across all panels. These spectrograms are computed from time-domain captures, not internal FPGA FFT taps or regenerated reference samples. Threshold-zero input and output STFT arrays are exactly equal. No new board execution was performed.",
    "host_workload_flute": "Historical warm-RAM host replay of physically captured FPGA sparse packets against host-derived same-threshold dense controls. Both implementations produce identical features. Left: medians of elapsed decode plus feature time. Right: medians and descriptive quartiles of the 30 paired dense/sparse ratios, not ratios of the displayed medians or confidence intervals. Threshold zero is an unfavorable sparse control. This does not measure FPGA-versus-laptop speedup, network, FFT/IFFT or AI inference. CPU identity applies only to this historical campaign.",
    "host_workload_monitor_replay": "Separate monitor revision02 software-reference timing campaign on four held-out five-second recordings. Plot shows complete receiver routes, 30 paired trials per recording and descriptive paired-ratio IQR. The median across the four per-recording paired median ratios is 1.31073049. The CPU model was not recorded; it must not be borrowed from the flute benchmark. Physical board output verification happened separately. No new timing or hardware execution.",
    "flute_waveform": "Recorded five-threshold physical flute waveform comparison. Original plot unchanged; removes 384 leading returned samples and uses common amplitude scales.",
    "flute_error_agreement": "Recorded input distortion versus exact threshold-specific reference agreement. Original numerical plot unchanged.",
    "flute_packet_sizes": "Recorded sparse TSP1 size versus the compact dense TSP1 baseline, not versus WAV or PCM. Original numerical plot unchanged.",
    "dv_topology": "Conceptual boundaries of oracle, host checking and physical capture. Original accepted diagram unchanged.",
    "dv_handshake": "Actual ModelSim ready/valid stall trace from the retained full-length threshold-zero simulation. Original plot unchanged; 10 ns simulation clock is distinct from nominal 20 ns board clock.",
    "dv_reset": "Actual ModelSim clear/reset excerpts during FFT and WOLA operation. Original plot unchanged; full recovery is checked by the separate scoreboard.",
    "dv_rounding": "Recorded old and repaired C++ responses for four rounded-shift boundary witnesses. Original plot unchanged."
  },
